WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.025
Check yourself with two questions.

2
00:00:02.025 --> 00:00:05.281
First: a contractor's
contract runs to January,

3
00:00:05.281 --> 00:00:09.137
but their sponsor recertification
was due in October.

4
00:00:09.137 --> 00:00:10.962
Which end does the extract use?

5
00:00:10.962 --> 00:00:16.413
The answer is b: the earliest condition
that applies, the recertification due date.

6
00:00:16.413 --> 00:00:20.313
The extract computes every end
condition and takes the first.

7
00:00:20.313 --> 00:00:23.787
Second: what does a C
R oh one finding mean?

8
00:00:23.787 --> 00:00:27.763
The answer is a: an enabled
account past its earliest end.

9
00:00:27.763 --> 00:00:31.399
An account with no register
record is the orphan,

10
00:00:31.399 --> 00:00:35.037
C R oh two, and a record with
no account is C R oh four.

11
00:00:35.037 --> 00:00:40.150
Once the disables are sent, the next
reconciliation shows no C R oh one.

12
00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:45.120
The module page has two more questions,
each linked to the section that answers it.
